('Why cleaner choice matters',P('Adult wellness products can be made from silicone, ABS plastic, glass, stainless steel, TPE, coated materials, or mixed powered parts. A single spray cannot be judged responsibly without knowing what it will touch. A cleaner that is fine for one smooth non-porous surface may be a poor match for a charging port, seam, porous sleeve, or decorative coating.','The goal is not to make shopping scary. It is to make the label do its job. A good product page tells adults what the cleaner is for, how to use it, when to rinse, and when not to use it. That is more valuable than loud sanitation language.')),
('Start with the toy material',P('Before buying cleaner, identify the toy material and whether the product is powered. Non-porous materials such as quality silicone, glass, and stainless steel are generally easier to clean than porous or uncertain materials, but the exact item still matters. Motors, seams, battery doors, suction openings, and textured areas need more care than a smooth solid item.','If the toy maker gives care instructions, those instructions should lead. Cleaner packaging should support that guidance rather than contradict it. When the toy material is unknown, be cautious and ask support before applying a new chemical product.')),
