('Rinsing, drying, and storage',P('Cleaning is only one step. Rinsing and drying often decide whether the product stays pleasant to use. If the cleaner requires rinsing, rinse fully and avoid leaving residue in seams or textured areas. Dry the toy completely before storage so lint, moisture, and packaging dyes do not create new problems.','A breathable drying spot, clean cloth, and separate storage pouch can be more useful than a complicated routine. Do not charge powered products while damp. Do not seal wet items in a pouch. Care should be repeatable, not heroic.')),
('Powered toys and water-resistance limits',P('Powered toys need extra attention because water-resistance ratings vary. A splash-resistant product may not be safe to submerge, and a cleaner spray can drift into seams or charging points. Look for clear care directions around buttons, ports, removable motors, and magnetic chargers.','If a listing uses waterproof casually, compare it with the toy’s real rating and instructions. IP ratings, when provided, describe tested conditions; they are not a promise that every cleaning method is safe forever.')),
